---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout section="Grant Types" title="OAuth 2.0 Grant Types &amp; Flows">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="learn-layout">
      <nav class="toc">
        <div class="toc-label">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#decision">Grant Type Decision Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="#auth-code">Authorization Code Flow (3-Legged)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#params-breakdown">Detailed Parameter Breakdown</a></li>
          <li><a href="#pkce">PKCE Extension (RFC 7636)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#client-creds">Client Credentials Flow (M2M)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#saml-assertion">SAML 2.0 Assertion Flow (RFC 7522)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#device">Device Authorization Flow (RFC 8628)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#interaction-code">Interaction Code Flow</a></li>
          <li><a href="#deprecated">Deprecated Flows (OAuth 2.1)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#refresh">Refresh Tokens &amp; Rotation</a></li>
        </ul>
        <hr class="toc-divider" />
        <nav class="toc-nav">
          <a href={base + '/oauth'}>&larr; OAuth 2.0</a>
          <a href={base + '/oidc'}>OIDC &rarr;</a>
        </nav>
      </nav>

      <main class="content">
        <div class="page-header">
          <span class="badge badge-intermediate">Intermediate &middot; 25 min</span>
          <h1>OAuth 2.0 Grant Types &amp; Flows</h1>
          <p class="lead">Deep dive into Authorization Code Flow with PKCE, M2M Client Credentials, SAML 2.0 Bearer assertions, Device Flow, and parameter breakdowns.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- DECISION GUIDE -->
        <section id="decision">
          <h2>Grant Type Decision Guide</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>App Type</th>
                <th>Client Type</th>
                <th>Recommended Flow</th>
                <th>Client Secret?</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Server-side Web App</strong> (Node, Python, Java)</td>
                <td>Confidential</td>
                <td>Authorization Code</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Single Page App</strong> (React, Vue, Angular)</td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Auth Code + PKCE</td>
                <td>No</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Mobile / Native App</strong> (iOS, Android)</td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Auth Code + PKCE</td>
                <td>No</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Microservice / Daemon / CLI</strong></td>
                <td>Confidential</td>
                <td>Client Credentials</td>
                <td>Yes</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>IoT / Smart TV / CLI Device</strong></td>
                <td>Public</td>
                <td>Device Authorization</td>
                <td>No</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <!-- AUTH CODE -->
        <section id="auth-code">
          <h2>Authorization Code Flow (Golden Standard - 3-Legged)</h2>
          <p>The 3-legged authorization code grant is the recommended standard for user authentication:</p>

          <pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as 👤 End User
    participant Client as 💻 Public Client (SPA / App)
    participant AuthServer as 🛡️ Authorization Server
    participant API as ⚡ Protected API / Gateway

    Note over Client: Generate code_verifier &amp; code_challenge (S256)
    Client-&gt;&gt;AuthServer: 1. GET /authorize?response_type=code&amp;code_challenge=...
    AuthServer-&gt;&gt;User: 2. Prompts Login &amp; Consent Screen
    User-&gt;&gt;AuthServer: 3. Submits Credentials &amp; Consents
    AuthServer--&gt;&gt;Client: 4. 302 Redirect with ?code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA&amp;state=...

    Note over Client,AuthServer: Back Channel Exchange
    Client-&gt;&gt;AuthServer: 5. POST /token (grant_type=authorization_code, code, code_verifier)
    Note over AuthServer: Verify SHA256(code_verifier) == code_challenge
    AuthServer--&gt;&gt;Client: 6. 200 OK &#123; access_token, id_token, refresh_token &#125;

    Client-&gt;&gt;API: 7. GET /api/resource (Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;)
    API--&gt;&gt;Client: 8. 200 OK (Protected JSON Data)
          </pre>
          
          <pre><code><span class="c">// STEP 1: Front Channel Authorization Request</span>
GET /authorize?
  response_type=code
  &amp;client_id=s6BhdRkqt3
  &amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fclient.example.com%2Fcb
  &amp;scope=openid%20profile%20email
  &amp;state=af0ifjsldkj HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com

<span class="c">// STEP 2: Front Channel Redirect Response (302 Found)</span>
HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: https://client.example.com/cb?
  code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA
  &amp;state=af0ifjsldkj

<span class="c">// STEP 3: Back Channel Token Request</span>
POST /token HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Basic czZCaGRSa3F0MzpnWDFmQmF0M2JW

grant_type=authorization_code
&amp;code=SplxlOBeZQQYbYS6WxSbIA
&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fclient.example.com%2Fcb
&amp;client_id=s6BhdRkqt3
&amp;client_secret=gX1fBat3bV

<span class="c">// STEP 4: Token Response JSON</span>
&#123;
  "access_token": "SlAV32hkKG",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600,
  "refresh_token": "8xLOxBtZp8",
  "scope": "openid profile email"
&#125;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- PARAMS BREAKDOWN -->
        <section id="params-breakdown">
          <h2>Detailed Parameter Breakdown</h2>
          
          <h3>1. GET /authorize Request Parameters</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><code>response_type=code</code>: Informs the Authorization Server that the application is requesting an authorization code grant.</li>
            <li><code>client_id</code>: Public identifier for the registered application.</li>
            <li><code>redirect_uri</code>: Whitelisted destination where the user browser will be redirected after approval.</li>
            <li><code>scope</code>: Space-separated list of requested permissions.</li>
            <li><code>state</code>: Cryptographically random string validated on return to prevent CSRF attacks.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>2. POST /token Request Parameters</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><code>grant_type=authorization_code</code>: Declares the token redemption grant type.</li>
            <li><code>code</code>: The single-use authorization code delivered in the redirect.</li>
            <li><code>redirect_uri</code>: Must match the exact redirect URI sent in the initial request.</li>
            <li><code>client_id</code> / <code>client_secret</code>: Confidential client credentials verifying the token requester's identity.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- PKCE -->
        <section id="pkce">
          <h2>PKCE Extension (RFC 7636)</h2>
          <p>Proof Key for Code Exchange prevents authorization code interception attacks on public clients:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Client creates a random <code>code_verifier</code> (43–128 URL-safe characters).</li>
            <li>Client calculates: <code>code_challenge = Base64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))</code>.</li>
            <li>Client sends <code>code_challenge</code> and <code>code_challenge_method=S256</code> in the front-channel <code>/authorize</code> request.</li>
            <li>Client presents original <code>code_verifier</code> in the back-channel <code>/token</code> POST request.</li>
            <li>Authorization Server validates: <code>SHA256(code_verifier) === code_challenge</code>.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- CLIENT CREDS -->
        <section id="client-creds">
          <h2>Client Credentials Flow (RFC 6749 Section 4.4)</h2>
          <p>Used for machine-to-machine (M2M) communication without an interactive user:</p>

          <pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Daemon as 🤖 Microservice / Daemon / CLI
    participant IdP as 🔑 Authorization Server
    participant API as 🗄️ Protected Backend API

    Note over Daemon,IdP: Direct Machine-to-Machine (No User Involved)
    Daemon-&gt;&gt;IdP: 1. POST /token (grant_type=client_credentials, client_id, client_secret)
    Note over IdP: Authenticate Client Secret &amp; Validate Scopes
    IdP--&gt;&gt;Daemon: 2. 200 OK &#123; access_token: "eyJ...", token_type: "Bearer", expires_in: 3600 &#125;

    Daemon-&gt;&gt;API: 3. GET /api/protected/reports (Authorization: Bearer eyJ...)
    Note over API: Verify JWT Signature (JWKS) &amp; Check Scopes
    API--&gt;&gt;Daemon: 4. 200 OK (Internal Reports JSON Payload)
          </pre>

          <pre><code>POST /token HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&amp;client_id=daemon_service_app
&amp;client_secret=secure_daemon_secret
&amp;scope=read:reports%20execute:jobs</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- SAML ASSERTION -->
        <section id="saml-assertion">
          <h2>SAML 2.0 Bearer Assertion Flow (RFC 7522)</h2>
          <p>Enables an enterprise client to exchange an existing signed SAML 2.0 XML assertion for an OAuth 2.0 access token:</p>
          <pre><code>POST /token HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Asaml2-bearer
&amp;assertion=PHNhbWxwOlJlc3BvbnNlIHhtbG5zOnNhbWxwPSJ1cm46b2FzaXM6bmFtZXM6dGM6U0FNTDoyLjA6cHJvdG9jb2wi...</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- DEVICE FLOW -->
        <section id="device">
          <h2>Device Authorization Flow (RFC 8628)</h2>
          <p>Designed for input-constrained devices (smart TVs, CLI tools):</p>
          <pre><code><span class="c">// 1. Device requests verification code</span>
POST /device/code HTTP/1.1
client_id=smart_tv_app

<span class="c">// Response</span>
&#123;
  "device_code": "GmRhmhcxhwAzkoEqiMEg...",
  "user_code": "WDJB-MJHT",
  "verification_uri": "https://example.com/activate",
  "interval": 5
&#125;</code></pre>
        </section>

        <!-- INTERACTION CODE -->
        <section id="interaction-code">
          <h2>Interaction Code Flow</h2>
          <p>An extension (supported by Okta Identity Engine) enabling client applications to natively drive authentication, passwordless challenges, and MFA interactions step-by-step without requiring full browser redirects.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- DEPRECATED -->
        <section id="deprecated">
          <h2>Deprecated Flows in OAuth 2.1</h2>
          <div class="callout danger">
            <strong>⛔ Deprecated in Modern Architecture:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Implicit Flow (<code>response_type=token</code>):</strong> Returns tokens directly in the URL fragment. High risk of token exposure in history, referer headers, and browser extensions. Replaced by Auth Code + PKCE.</li>
              <li><strong>Resource Owner Password Flow (<code>grant_type=password</code>):</strong> Re-introduces the password anti-pattern by asking applications to collect master user credentials directly. Avoid in all modern architectures.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- REFRESH -->
        <section id="refresh">
          <h2>Refresh Tokens &amp; Rotation (RFC 6749 Section 6)</h2>
          <pre><code>POST /token HTTP/1.1
Host: authorization-server.example.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token
&amp;refresh_token=tGzv3JOkF0XG5Qx2TlKWIA</code></pre>
          <p><strong>Refresh Token Rotation:</strong> Every time a refresh token is used, the Authorization Server invalidates it and issues a fresh refresh token pair. If a revoked token is presented, the server revokes the entire session lineage.</p>
        </section>

        <footer class="page-footer">
          <div class="prev-next">
            <a href={base + '/oauth'}>&larr; OAuth 2.0</a>
            <a href={base + '/oidc'}>Next: OIDC &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
